                <pb facs="0832" n="1666" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/518</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-07T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 8, 6.13
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1052. Referring to the Embassy’s No. 1049, February 5, 11 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d710-f1"/> French
                    financial delegate Lasteyrie, associate of Mauclère, leaves to-night for Paris,
                    Spanish conferees having declined further to discuss French-Spanish financial
                    agreement pending Department’s final decision concerning our tentative agreement
                    (Embassy’s 1029, January 30, 10 a.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d710-f2"/>).</p>
                <p>Lasteyrie frankly stated that France is without money or securities and that
                    unless she can obtain credit, she must stop all purchases in Spain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
